    "updated_at": "2020-08-19T07:25:20Z",
    "body": "Interesting. This is almost certainly caused by something attempting to invoke Java when it's not actually installed.\r\n\r\nJust to confirm, does this happen in every directory, or does it only happen when you enter a directory where a java \"triggering file\" exists?\r\n\r\nThe \"triggering files\" for Java are:\r\n- pom.xml, build.gradle.kts, build.sbt or .java-version \r\n- Any file with a .java, .class, .gradle or .jar extension",
