    "created_at": "2020-08-19T07:30:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-19T07:34:57Z",
    "body": "Hi @Tarang, I think what is happening here is that there is something in that directory that is triggering the Java module, the Java module then execute java to try to get the version, if you don't have java installed macOS will prompt you to install it (this is the prompt you are seeing). A quick fix would be to disable the Java module by running `starship configure java.disabled true` or adding the following to you starship config file.\r\n\r\n```toml\r\n[java]\r\ndisabled = true\r\n```",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
