    "updated_at": "2020-08-19T08:39:28Z",
    "body": "Thanks that fixes it.\r\n\r\nI'm not quite sure actually, it wouldn't actually show up on a specific folder it would if i pressed up for some bash history. I wasn't quite sure what was causing it. My project directory was a rust application with no java files in it. I do have some java applications on my laptop but i was not browsing the directory containing them when this was happening.\r\n\r\nI think it might be better to test for a java install instead of explicitly disabling it specifically to stop the prompt from showing up again and again. It's just the prompt that is very naggy. Initially i thought it was another application but it would only happen with the terminal and thats how i narrowed it down to starship as it was the only new tool i had installed.",
