    "created_at": "2020-08-19T09:00:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-08-19T09:00:53Z",
    "body": "This is a bit of an edge-case that probably only exists on macOS. There is always a `java` binary available on the PATH, because Apple adds a shim that pops up that installation request. So it is not enough for Starship to check if `java` exists and can be run, it needs to check that `java` is actually Java 🤦‍♀️ \r\n\r\n`/usr/libexec/java_home` is [apparently what you would want to use](https://stackoverflow.com/a/44158166). (I would open a PR, but I am not a Rust programmer.)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
